-- ============================================================================
-- RC7 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Well Test Analysis, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions. Structure generated from the tier's
-- manifest.json.
--
-- What this tier owns: the regression, and the class of error it introduces.
-- Log-space residuals with the derivative in them; bounded, log-scaled
-- parameters and the skin floor the catalog imposes on every model but the
-- homogeneous one; a fit that recovers the planted 85 mD, 6.5 skin and 0.015
-- bbl/psi storage to six significant figures where the best straight line was
-- three percent low. Then what a fit cannot tell you: a 95 percent interval
-- five parts in a billion wide that measures the optimiser rather than the
-- reservoir; a sealing-fault model fitted to a boundary-free buildup that
-- converges on a fault at about three thousand feet and MOVES IT 116 ft, to a
-- non-overlapping interval, when the same pressure change is written an
-- arithmetically equivalent way differing by 4.547473508864641e-13 psi; and a
-- dual-porosity model that degenerates to the right answer at a bound and
-- reports failure. Then rate history, gas pseudo-pressure and deliverability,
-- and rate transient analysis for oil, gas and linear flow.
--
-- Module m06 carries the course's refusals: deconvolution, interference and
-- multi-well testing, and the separation of a gas well's apparent skin into
-- its Darcy and non-Darcy parts. All three are taught with their mechanisms
-- and their value stated, and none of them is graded. The go-live migration
-- ASSERTS that, refusing to run if any capstone field key mentions them.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

values ('welltest', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-regression","title":"Regression","lesson_keys":["l01-from-straight-line-to-model","l02-residuals-in-log-space","l03-bounds-and-the-skin-floor","l04-what-the-line-could-not-recover"]},{"key":"m02-what-a-fit-cannot-tell-you","title":"What a Fit Cannot Tell You","lesson_keys":["l01-a-confidence-interval-on-clean-data","l02-the-phantom-fault","l03-a-model-that-degenerates","l04-reporting-a-match-honestly"]},{"key":"m03-rate-history","title":"Rate History","lesson_keys":["l01-superposition-properly","l02-the-equivalent-producing-time","l03-multi-rate-semilog","l04-what-ignoring-the-history-costs"]},{"key":"m04-gas","title":"Gas","lesson_keys":["l01-why-pressure-squared-is-not-enough","l02-pseudo-pressure","l03-the-equivalent-liquid-adapter","l04-deliverability","l05-two-answers-from-three-points"]},{"key":"m05-rate-transient-analysis","title":"Rate Transient Analysis","lesson_keys":["l01-production-data-as-a-test","l02-material-balance-time","l03-the-flowing-material-balance","l04-gas-and-pseudo-time","l05-the-product-you-cannot-split"]},{"key":"m06-the-expert-reading","title":"The Expert Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-what-this-course-will-not-certify","l03-working-the-capstone","l04-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
